/ Attribution lines under an address cell: reverse DNS, then
/ country · AS number · AS name - whatever the IpEnrichment cache holds
/ (the same CymruLookup data the honeypot pages show). Renders nothing
/ for an address not yet looked up; the page's refresh loop fills it in
/ once the background lookup lands.
- if ip && (enr = @enrichments[ip]&.with_indifferent_access)
  - if enr[:rdns]
    .text-xs.font-mono.font-normal.break-all.text-slate-500.dark:text-slate-400= enr[:rdns]
  - if enr[:country] || enr[:asn] || enr[:as_name]
    .text-xs.font-sans.font-normal.text-slate-500.dark:text-slate-400
      = [ enr[:country], ("AS#{enr[:asn]}" if enr[:asn]), enr[:as_name] ].compact.join(" · ")
